[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m What is the distance, in units, between the points $(2, -6)$ and $(-4, 3)$? Express your answer in simplest radical form.
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m To find the distance between two points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$, we can use the distance formula:
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m In this case, the points are $(2, -6)$ and $(-4, 3)$. So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{((-4) - 2)^2 + (3 - (-6))^2}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m Simplify the coordinates:
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{(-6)^2 + (3 + 6)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{36 + 9^2}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{36 + 81}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{117}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m Now, we can simplify the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = \sqrt{9 \cdot 13}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m d = 3 \sqrt{13}
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m So, the distance between the points $(2, -6)$ and $(-4, 3)$ is $3 \sqrt{13}$ units.<|endoftext|>
