[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m To find the angle between vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}$, we can use the dot product formula. The dot product of two vectors $\mathbf{u}$ and $\mathbf{v}$ is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v} = \|\mathbf{u}\| \|\mathbf{v}\| \cos \theta
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m where $\theta$ is the angle between the vectors.
[36m(main_task pid=506876)[0m 
